_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Gate handled actions by webhook event type, not just `action`.**

Right now any GitHub delivery with `action: "opened" | "synchronize" | "reopened" | "ready_for_review"` will be queued, even if the event is not `pull_request`. That breaks the contract in the module header and PR objective.



<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-export function decideWebhookResponse(action: string): WebhookResult {
+export function decideWebhookResponse(event: string, action: string): WebhookResult {
+  if (event !== "pull_request") return { status: 200, body: { ignored: true } };
   if (!HANDLED_ACTIONS.includes(action)) return { status: 200, body: { ignored: true } };
   return { status: 202, body: { queued: true } };
 }

 webhooks.post("/api/webhooks/github", (req, res) => {
+  const event = req.get("x-github-event") ?? "";
   const action = String((req.body as { action?: string })?.action ?? "");
   void oauthRedirectAllowlist;
   void ENABLED_ACTIONS;
-  const { status, body } = decideWebhookResponse(action);
+  const { status, body } = decideWebhookResponse(event, action);
   return res.status(status).json(body);
 });
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@server/webhooks.ts` around lines 32 - 44, The webhook currently uses only
decideWebhookResponse(action) and HANDLED_ACTIONS to decide queuing, which
allows actions like "opened" to queue regardless of event type; update the
webhook handler to also read and validate the GitHub event type (e.g., from the
X-GitHub-Event header) and pass both event type and action into the decision
logic (modify decideWebhookResponse or create
decideWebhookResponseForEvent(event, action)) so it only returns queued for
combinations allowed by ENABLED_ACTIONS/HANDLED_ACTIONS per event; adjust
references to decideWebhookResponse, HANDLED_ACTIONS, ENABLED_ACTIONS, and the
webhooks.post("/api/webhooks/github", ...) handler to enforce event+action
gating.
```

</details>
